{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small","id":1097592,"title":"Lunar Exalted and the power of being small","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T12:49:45-07:00","id":1097592,"title":"Lunar Exalted and the power of being small","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">SHAPESHIFTING (excerpts)</span><br /> <br /> A Lunar may pay four motes to assume any form it has taken. This transformation lasts indefinitely, until the Lunar reverts to his true human form (which is free and reflexive) or shifts into a different shape. Shapeshifting can be flurried, but not with an attack.<br /> <br /> Animals with Legendary Size are beyond the skill of most young Lunar shapeshifters, though this limitation can be overcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">DEXTERITY CHARMS (ideas)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Humble Mouse Shape </b><br /> This presumes that the power to don the form of a creature with the Tiny Creature merit is initially locked, like Legendary Size. As a reminder, this merit belongs to most creatures at least as small as a house-cat, granting them +2 Evasion against larger foes. Larger characters must also subtract two successes from any Awareness-based roll made to notice a Tiny Creature.<br /> <br /> <b>Rat's Head Technique</b><br /> Essentially a mirror of Solar &quot;Door-Evading Technique&quot;, but it requires the Lunar to be at least as small as a mouse. The Lunar twists and shrinks as much as necessary to squeeze through any barred passage. Dealing with locks as per &quot;Lock-Opening Touch&quot; is an entirely separate matter that Lunars will have to approach from a different direction.<br /> <br /> <b>Stealthy Fox Method</b><br /> If the Lunar attempts to go to ground in combat in the form of a Tiny Creature, when all his opponents are larger than house-cats, the penalty for doing so begins at -0 instead of -3.<br /> <br /> <b>Traceless Passage Technique</b><br /> While in a form with the Tiny Creature merit, the Lunar ignores the -3 penalty to Stealth rolls for moving while concealed. Alternatively, she can apply this Charm to a single Survival roll to conceal her tracks, gaining (Essence) automatic successes and is bolstered by the double 9s rule. The Lunar cannot be tracked conventionally, not even with the aid of tracking animals or other means\u2014mundane attempts automatically fail. Only those with supernatural prowess can hope to find the vanished Lunar.<br /> <br /> <b>Emerald Grasshopper Form</b><br /> The Lunar can reflexively assume any form at least as small as a house-cat, potentially gaining the benefits of Tiny Creature's Evasion bonus against an attack after it has been declared.<br /> <br /> <b>Becoming the Swarm</b><br /> The Lunar subdivides his body into a swarm of lesser creatures, or multiplies from one small creature into many. These creatures individually may be no larger than a house-cat. The Lunar is free to mix and match species in the swarm, but if he wishes to use unconventional forms of locomotion (such as flight or crawling up walls) all creatures comprising the swarm must be capable of such movement. The Lunar adds half of the Dexterity rating (rounded up) of the swarm's primary species to his Evasion against attacks that are not large enough to encompass the entire range band. This bonus counts as non-Charm dice and can stack with the bonus of Tiny Creature.<br /> <br /> Becoming the Swarm is explicitly allowed to combine with Ant and Starfish Trick (mirror of Solar &quot;Faster Than Self Technique&quot;), allowing the Lunar to become a swarm large enough to constitute a battle group.<br /> <br /> <b>Agitation of the Swarm</b><br /> The Lunar supplements a Distraction gambit with his swarm-form, using his dispersed mass and irritating assaults to conceal the approaching attack of an ally.<br /> <br /> <b>Swinging At Flies</b><br /> Upon successfully dodging an attack with an Evasion Defense that employed the Tiny Creature merit, the Lunar can retroactively and reflexively activate Becoming the Swarm. She dodged the attack via becoming too numerous as well as too small to strike.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dancing Beneath Giant's Feet</b><br /> A dice-trick Charm that improves upon the Evasion bonus of the Tiny Creature merit, or alternatively allows the Lunar to enjoy similar bonuses against a creature of Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> <b>Wasp Sting Blur</b><br /> A dice-trick or counter-attack Charm that the Lunar can use against an opponent who failed to strike him thanks to Dancing Beneath Giant's Feet.<br /> <br /> <b>Climbing the Giant</b><br /> A special grappling maneuver which leaves a larger victim completely unhindered versus anyone else, but heavily penalizes his attacks against the clinging Lunar, while also making it effectively impossible to Disengage from the Lunar.<br /> <br /> <b>Giant Swats His Face</b><br /> The Lunar activates this Charm in response to a failed attack from the victim of &quot;Climbing the Giant&quot;, causing the victim to hurt himself instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Swallow A Spider</b><br /> The Lunar invades the body of a victim of &quot;Climbing the Giant&quot;, entering through a nostril or mouth or some other orifice. A different and much more destructive form of grapple, with the Slam maneuver representing the Lunar shapeshifting into a larger form to burst out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:16:20-07:00","id":1097673,"title":"","content":"All of these Concepts are great. I am however dissatisfied by their nu!ber. I want us to avoid air-breathing mermaid I suppose.<br /> <br /> The problem is shape-shifting is a very powerful and versatile tool but without mechanics to back up an action you're going to defaults to the general guidance that the system gives you. I don't understand the Third Edition...<br /> But traditionally if it wasn't done with a charm or it wasn't the focus of a charm you could be taking an action as described and it would have ridiculously minor effects.<br /> Such as for instance blinding an opponent taking off of your Four dice as opposed to have any charm called I am undetectable that would make them literally untargetable by anyone suffering from it.<br /> <br /> This allows for game balance, especially given the collectible card game origins of the charm system<br /> You avoid someone having extra power for buying one power. Discreet and effective powers are very nice especially as they're easy to memorize but powerful when used in combination if you can organize.<br /> <br /> Is there a way that we can condense all of these effects into just a few charms for the lunar exalted with the understanding that it's possible<br /> <br /> The entire giant climbing tree, for instance, sounds like something that really shouldn't be a charm the series of strategies that would open up with the right form.<br /> <br /> But at the same time I can understand putting peculiar rules and systems in just for the lunars can be detrimental and it's always nice to have all your special effects Under One Roof as a gamer with an RPG supplement<br /> <br /> So yes I would want these c harms to be effectively more powerful by having fewer of them so that each few number do a lot of each of these things<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of concept or something I don't want... it's probably becoming the Swarm mainly because I associated with that weird travel spell<br /> <br /> I don't know it just feels as if it's a cheat that a lunar can literally do a celestrial level spell with their native Magic<br /> <br /> My fix for it would actually mean to make swarm charm more powerful in a way. Instead of just being a special effect the lunar would literally create a large number of bodies out of his Mass of whatever tiny creature he makes.<br /> The catch? these creatures are real. they may all be effective clones or series of variations within the same genetic code or your hearts blood<br /> They would certainly all be Supernaturally loyal the lunar being an effective hive or pack mind or what have you<br /> But they would all be real.<br /> And yes the lunar could shape-shift into their proper form though maybe as a slight disincentive make it so that they have to spend however many stamina points in difference as motes to make up for the Lost Mass unless they can get 80% of the original family back in order form their whole body. They're technobabble reasons for why this doesn't apply to normal small shape-shifting basically because technically you traded a large thing for a small thing getting the large thing back is easy but here you traded a large thing for many small things so to get the large thing back you have to pay more.<br /> <br /> The good news is that technically he's created several hundred decoys to act as abalative shielding. Bad news is that as they are animals they are going to be vulnerable to various social attacks and survival charms or even just tricks such as whatever it is that we use to keep our scare away mice cats or dogs. If you use your personal terms to enhance one that's where your mind and soul is otherwise until you do that you exist as a spirit amongst the Swarm and not out of body either. The swarm is your body as the combination or cells and tissues and symbiotic organisms are your true form.<br /> <br /> Inshort lunar power at shape-shifting works too well. It's not an effect it's an actual thing that happens.<br /> However I also understand why that would be detrimental with a charm effectively having a negative draw back or requiring more difficulty in order to use.<br /> Edit to add<br /> thinking more on Swarm make it actually based off the mass of the creature they are relative to the creatures they are becoming.<br /> It would probably be something like you need to be able to separate in it to at least a dozen of the target based on the mass difference.<br /> This does mean that a lunar can then shape-shift into an elephant and then swarm into a series of tigers or men. Only with the abilities of the lunar and the raw attributes with no real thoughts originating in themselves but a strong intimacy and motive based on the direction of the lunar when they activate swarming. They can change it but that's more of a social attack though it would probably be peternaturally easy like an eclipse that can do ugh that perfectly talk with body language charm. Only one success needed to change intimacy and motivations and deep characters and make them as complex and well understood as possible these are after all multiple clones or buds off of your own mind<br /> <br /> Well that's for humans. tigers will just behave like tigerslead by a shared Spirit. The problem is the longer that they live the more their souls develop and the more individuality they develop. Animals will have a sort of instinct will memory from the lunar and of course the victim that the lunar ate. Peoplet copies will only know language and skills but otherwise be amnesiac if they last for longer than a scene or so as they develop their own soul/psyche<br /> <br /> As for why this doesn't change the balance of power? For pretty much the same reason why you can't build an army out of clones or is society all of the same person.<br /> And they can't make an effective Army because practically you're going to go from drones to the equivalent of a rebellious teenaged mob in a few days. Also if there are new Souls being developed in an area chances are that means some Spirit or God or fey is going to want in on that action<br /> <br /> This might lead to lunars being able to pay off Fey Folk by themselves if they just want flesh or blood or bones. But these things don't have their own dreams their own experiences they're relatively shallow in and of themselves at the soul.<br /> <br /> a rakasha might still want them. Or guild slaver. It also adds to the legend of the lunars because some people will think if they see multiple of a person or of a certain tribe that they might be a fetch or a plant by a lunar and until they've killed the tribes God they can't trust or take them as slaves<br /> <br /> Sorry my imagination gets away from me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 05-27-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:51:21-07:00","id":1097679,"title":"","content":"Even without charms, I think Odo has shown us the power of using small forms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T22:15:15-07:00","id":1097692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097673#post1097673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want us to avoid air-breathing mermaid I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do I, but Swallow A Spider is very deliberately an air-breathing mermaid Charm, because doing that kind of thing all of the time is a bit much, and significant opponents should have plenty of opportunity to defend against it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Climbing the Giant, on the other hand, might not be so necessary.<br /> <br /> Giant Swats His Face absolutely needs a Charm, because redirecting an attack is beyond the level of a stunt or gambit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a way that we can condense all of these effects into just a few charms for the lunar exalted with the understanding that it's possible </div> </div> </div>You might as well ask if we can condense all of the newer, humbler Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of concept or something I don't want... it's probably becoming the Swarm mainly because I associated with that weird travel spell<br /> <br /> I don't know it just feels as if it's a cheat that a lunar can literally do a celestrial level spell with their native Magic </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure that the Spell must be stronger than this effect, though I think I goofed in making its Defense bonus not count against the dice-adder limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T23:42:21-07:00","id":1097699,"title":"","content":"I think I misremembered the spell is terrestrial and remember I'm more of a first edition aficionado<br /> <br /> Basically it's rather inefficient and compared to later movement charms not really that good. It causes your body to split into a flock of birds or raitons and transports you some distance away.<br /> <br /> I understand the appeal of making that an actual maneuver that shapeshifters can do, at the very least being able to pull some mr. fantastic style dodges.<br /> <br /> <br /> Making the charm or relatively small charm tree into a collection of abilities that at the same time create as much complications as they do advantages strikes me as a great trade-off to make the swarm charms distinct from the spell.<br /> <br /> With a spell you do become Birds but they don't really matter it's just a Teleport effect with some really cool decals. With Swarm charms you are actually creating a mass amount of life, but you're creating a mass amount of <i>life</i>. Sure that's an advantage for the magical lunar Trickster totem warrior, but life is always complicated and demanding and costly.<br /> <br /> You know I would actually disagree on the idea that you need to put a charm cost on the stop hitting yourself or the orifice entrance. I'd assume that defending against such is exceptionally easy.Reflexive bites, or clinching of orifices to block holes and create more contested rolls. The inherit drawback after all is that you can't do this while you're in your 16 Strength 18 armed &amp; dexterity build but in the form of a mouse or a spider. You are trading a grapple for pinching. Giving yourself and your opponent Mobility and losing hardiness. Your tiny form will naturally have very low defense, be very vulnerable and you are actually sacrificing your difficulty to be hit by directly touching someone. A terrestrial exalted can easily kill you just by contact. Heck even a solar could probably stunt a blinding or sensory overload effect just by flaring their anima. And the most common basic defense of wear clothing/coverage. Let's not even get into what a lunar or Fair folk could excrete or turn their skin into.<br /> <br /> Moreover what's the stop someone that you're trying to jump down the mouth of from vomiting you out hacking you out or actually eating you. Or drowning you in some thick poison that they're currently immune to or just a lot of highproof wine that hurts you thanks to your low body weight?<br /> Of course a lunar will be able to compensate for this by having their own soak or dexterity or whatever charms. But that strikes me as no worse than someone investing in a particular martial arts style. (again I don't understand Third Edition.) <br /> <br /> You can't just throw on some tiger claws and go, &quot;I use tiger style to defeat my enemies.&quot; you usually have to invest in the right attributes, get a large amount of the charm tree and have supplementary natural charms to make sure that you are exceptionally good at a very specific version of fighting along with the right artifacts.<br /> I don't think its too threatening that a setting where lunars can do this means that, for me, it's something that inhabitants have to think about and consider when they're fighting or, more accurately, when they're living their lives. Also solar's already have a charm to deal with invasive pests three of them technically hardship surviving mendicant spirit, immunity to everything, and hypnotic tongue technique after all if you were touching them<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh well I guess it really does depend on aims and effectiveness.<br /> I think making it so that something is more inherent in the actions that are taken is better than gating them behind charms.<br /> This prevents something were New charm spaces and Technologies develop in later material that open up a line that you need to be competitive in in order to never fall behind. But your charmset wasn't designed for it. In first edition sometimes this was the leaping dodges and midbattle feints or tricks that charms about those actions were made to not reliably work in battle. Another example of necessary post established charm tech would be the targeting or crippling charms that became apart of martial arts and then later Abyssals trees. Apparently learning how to disable your opponent by doing damage to a limb was something that only the darkest murderers could get by selling their souls to monsters from beneath the void. \ud83d\ude44::rolleyes::<br /> <br /> Making it so that you have a system for what happens when a small fighter takes on an exceptionally larger fighter means that you not only give a system for when Lunars try to become Mighty Mouse or Reepicheep. Or... (I think I'm forgetting some heroic bug folk hero or something...)<br /> But it also prepares all Exalted for when they eventually get into the type of battles where it's relevant. This is likely to happen as little guy versus giant monster is starting to become a lot more of a fad thanks to Dark Souls, Attack on Titan, god of war and so on.<br /> <br /> What are peculiar situations that seem unique to Lunar Exalted may very well end up situations that any Exalted could benefit from having firm system approach in.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":".  Clarifying and presentation editting for Sunder the Gold. 05-28-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:42:22-07:00","id":1097786,"title":"","content":"Darmani, please uses more paragraph breaks. One after each paragraph, and two between sections.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, how would people feel if Flowing Body Evasion and Becoming Water's Envy -- the Lunar perfect dodge Charms -- were tied into the idea of becoming a swarm of little creatures?<br /> <br /> No one can be as fast as the Solar Exalted can be, so everyone else approached perfect dodging in their own unique ways. Dragon-Blooded dissolved into an element, Alchemicals became immaterial, Sidereal Exalted re-wrote reality to be somewhere else... and the Lunar Exalted don't do &quot;rubber man body-stretching&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> So I figure that Bayonetta's &quot;I'm a bunch of butterflies&quot; dodge is probably what the Lunar Exalted ought to be doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:50:59-07:00","id":1097789,"title":"","content":"For the latter, perhaps, but the way I see Flowing Body Evasion, perhaps they just evade <i>really well</i>? Batman was able to dodge Darkseid's eye beams without stretching his body into rubber <i>or</i> turning into butterflies, and fucking <i>Superman</i> has been tagged by them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:12:48-07:00","id":1097795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097789#post1097789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the latter, perhaps, but the way I see Flowing Body Evasion, perhaps they just evade <i>really well</i>? Batman was able to dodge Darkseid's eye beams without stretching his body into rubber <i>or</i> turning into butterflies, and fucking <i>Superman</i> has been tagged by them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is a complicated kettle of fish in the Exalted context. There's always an argument about whether he's a Solar or a mortal.<br /> <br /> And sure, Lunar Exalted could just be really fast... but weren't <i>you </i>the one complaining about &quot;Silver Solar Syndrome&quot; in the other thread? Why wouldn't you want the Lunar Exalted to achieve their splat-defining perfect dodge in a completely different way from the Solar Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:48:37-07:00","id":1097801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097795#post1097795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman is a complicated kettle of fish in the Exalted context. There's always an argument about whether he's a Solar or a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is Batman, and in this context he's an example of a person who is very good at getting out of the way of an attack, which is something <i>any</i> splat can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097795#post1097795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sure, Lunar Exalted could just be really fast... but weren't <i>you </i>the one complaining about &quot;Silver Solar Syndrome&quot; in the other thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I was advising against basing your hypothetical Lunar Charm entirely off an existing Solar Charm. &quot;Dodge&quot; is <i>not</i> a single Solar Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097795#post1097795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't you want the Lunar Exalted to achieve their splat-defining perfect dodge in a completely different way from the Solar Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because to some degree, I have to be able to project myself into the character I play, and it's hard to get into the head of a character who has an easier time of avoiding an attack by turning into a swarm of butterflies <i>than just dodging it</i>. <br /> <br /> I don't particularly care if they're Ability-based, Attribute-based, viewed through the lens of the elements or the Maidens or Ten Sheaves - the Exalted are human first, so the first Charms they learn in a given tree shouldn't look <i>too</i> different from the mortal way of doing things, and for enhancing Evasion, that's &quot;dodge the attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Man, all this talk about dodging is making me want to watch DBZ Abridged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-28-2017, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:33:18-07:00","id":1097818,"title":"","content":"Hmm...making their perfect dodge predicated on turning into a bunch of creatures possibly works, but they might need alternatives to deal with things that could hit the entire swarm at once like avalanches and massive explosions. The solution there might be some sort of &quot;survive anything&quot; Stamina Charm instead of Dexterity stuff, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T12:29:20-07:00","id":1097843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097801#post1097801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the first Charms they learn in a given tree shouldn't look <i>too</i> different from the mortal way of doing things</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Edition's Seven Shadow Evasion is.. NOT a ground-level Charm. You need to buy three other Charms, first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Batman is Batman, and in this context he's an example of a person who is very good at getting out of the way of an attack, which is something <i>any</i> splat can be. </div> </div> </div>But only Solar Exalted have a perfect dodge that works just by being impossibly agile.<br /> <br /> Like I said, Dragon-Blooded need to transform themselves bodily into their elements to let danger pass through them. Alchemical Exalted use a device to become immaterial. Sidereal Exalted re-write reality. Abyssal and Infernal Exalted are essentially Solar Exalted. Getimians will likely hack reality, and Liminal Exalted will likely break and bend their bodies in grotesque ways to avoid worse harm.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted have plenty of other opportunities to be fast without needing to rely on speed for this trick. (In fact, they've never relied solely on being agile for this trick. The Charm has always implied that their bodies needed to literally flow like water to make it happen.)<br /> <br /> If Batman is a Dragon-Blood, he needs to become water or air to perfect dodge. If he's a Lunar, it only makes sense that Batman would perfectly dodge an attack by turning into a swarm of bats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because to some degree, I have to be able to project myself into the character I play, and it's hard to get into the head of a character who has an easier time of avoiding an attack by turning into a swarm of butterflies <i>than just dodging it</i>. </div> </div> </div>Literally no one has complained about a Fire Aspect Terrestrial needing to turn into a pillar of fire to allow an unblockable, undodgeable attack with uncountable damage to pass harmlessly through his personal space. Why would Bayonetta's butterfly dodge be a problem for Lunar Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:17:47-07:00","id":1097907,"title":"","content":"Heh. &quot;Perfect orbit, my ass!&quot; Okay, I'm back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition's Seven Shadow Evasion is.. NOT a ground-level Charm. You need to buy three other Charms, first.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about Seven Shadow Evasion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But only Solar Exalted have a perfect dodge that works just by being impossibly agile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does Flowing Body Evasion need to be perfect? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, Dragon-Blooded need to transform themselves bodily into their elements to let danger pass through them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and stay with me on this, they'd hop out of the way, or they'd weave out of the path of the attack in such a way as to cause it to target an ally. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemical Exalted use a device to become immaterial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall Precalculated Evasion System all that well, but I didn't think it made you immaterial. And even if that's the case, prior Charms still had you moving your body to not get hit by attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Exalted re-write reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avoidance Kata teleported the Sidereal, but Duck Fate was just a really good dodge. I also wouldn't describe either as &quot;re-write reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he's a Lunar, it only makes sense that Batman would perfectly dodge an attack by turning into a swarm of bats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already said that was a fine way to do the second Charm, but <i>why does Batman need two perfect dodges involving turning into a swarm of bats?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally no one has complained about a Fire Aspect Terrestrial needing to turn into a pillar of fire to allow an unblockable, undodgeable attack with uncountable damage to pass harmlessly through his personal space.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of them were probably upset that Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode (a Charm where a Dragon-Blooded <i>perfectly defends against an attack <b>by just moving his sword</b></i>) was so shitty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Bayonetta's butterfly dodge be a problem for Lunar Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't put words in my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:30:13-07:00","id":1097912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097907#post1097907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're not talking about Seven Shadow Evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your point makes even less sense. Why would you assume that the Lunar perfect dodge Charm would lack any prerequisites? Or ANY perfect dodge Charm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does Flowing Body Evasion need to be perfect? </div> </div> </div>...What do you really want?<br /> <br /> Seriously, what are you trying to do, here? This can't be sincere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:42:41-07:00","id":1097916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097912#post1097912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...What do you really want?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to buy two Charms that achieve the exact same thing the exact same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097912#post1097912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, what are you trying to do, here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally, have the littlest bit of say regarding what Lunars can be, by weighing in on the ideas of others, since my spirits are seldom high enough to start a thread of my own to share my ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097912#post1097912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can't be sincere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:54:09-07:00","id":1097920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097843#post1097843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition's Seven Shadow Evasion is.. NOT a ground-level Charm. You need to buy three other Charms, first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But only Solar Exalted have a perfect dodge that works just by being impossibly agile.<br /> <br /> Like I said, Dragon-Blooded need to transform themselves bodily into their elements to let danger pass through them. Alchemical Exalted use a device to become immaterial. Sidereal Exalted re-write reality. Abyssal and Infernal Exalted are essentially Solar Exalted. Getimians will likely hack reality, and Liminal Exalted will likely break and bend their bodies in grotesque ways to avoid worse harm.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted have plenty of other opportunities to be fast without needing to rely on speed for this trick. (In fact, they've never relied solely on being agile for this trick. The Charm has always implied that their bodies needed to literally flow like water to make it happen.)<br /> <br /> If Batman is a Dragon-Blood, he needs to become water or air to perfect dodge. If he's a Lunar, it only makes sense that Batman would perfectly dodge an attack by turning into a swarm of bats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Literally no one has complained about a Fire Aspect Terrestrial needing to turn into a pillar of fire to allow an unblockable, undodgeable attack with uncountable damage to pass harmlessly through his personal space. Why would Bayonetta's butterfly dodge be a problem for Lunar Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that fire thing is new. Also the fact what is likely inspiring it just uses it for a nice visual trick ala Bayonetta's dodge. Afterall if Bayonetta can perfectly ignore wind disturbance and become a swarm why doesn't she just FLY through all barriers and doors.<br /> <br /> If Lunars can do something that radical making it so.. specific...<br /> <br /> Also, frankly. I don't think you need to rethink *everything* for the Lunar Exalted. The first charms will be about contortion or just speed, awareness and dodging. Its later they do swarm shit.<br /> that's my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T02:04:48-07:00","id":1098035,"title":"","content":"I like all the concepts here, and don't really have criticisms because Lunars are my favorite splat and the charms displayed here are making me really want to play a Lunar with these Charms. I like the Swarm ones. They've always been a thematic and conceptual pick for me back in 2E iirc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1097920#post1097920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that fire thing is new. Also the fact what is likely inspiring it just uses it for a nice visual trick ala Bayonetta's dodge. Afterall if Bayonetta can perfectly ignore wind disturbance and become a swarm why doesn't she just FLY through all barriers and doors.<br /> <br /> If Lunars can do something that radical making it so.. specific...<br /> <br /> Also, frankly. I don't think you need to rethink *everything* for the Lunar Exalted. The first charms will be about contortion or just speed, awareness and dodging. Its later they do swarm shit.<br /> that's my guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Darmani here. Lower Essence charms begin with more human stuff. Contortion/speed. Higher levels become transformation and swarms. Like how lower level Solar Charms are moving really quickly away to turning into Shadow or not having been hit in the first place. Fits in thematically, and makes it so the cool stuff isn't always just found in the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12881-coffeegalaxies","name":"coffeegalaxies","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:20:47-07:00","id":1098137,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-Blooded perfect dodge Charm is only &quot;new&quot; in the sense that they didn't <i>have </i>anything of the sort until their manual in Second Edition was printed 11 years ago.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have NO IDEA where these complaints of &quot;lower Essence Charms&quot; are even coming from. Nothing in the first post suggests that Becoming the Swarm would be a low Essence Charm; it was <b>Essence 4 </b>in Glories: Luna, so even with rejiggering for 3rd Edition, I doubt it would be Essence 1.<br /> <br /> Neither does that complaint make any sense as a justification for why the Lunar perfect dodge shouldn't be &quot;break apart into a swarm and reform when safe&quot;, as I doubt Lunars can get perfect dodges with less Charm investment than Solar Exalted. There's plenty of room for Lunar Exalted to have &quot;I'm just that fast&quot; for some dodge Charms before the perfect dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:12:55-07:00","id":1098155,"title":"","content":"That's one of those puzzles where you only see the picture when you put it together - if Becoming the Swarm and other &quot;become a swarm&quot; tricks are the territory of high-Essence Charms, <i>and </i>Lunars need to become a swarm to perfect dodge stuff, then <b>Lunars in your model won't be able to perfect dodge stuff until they're high-Essence</b>.<br /> <br /> \u200bSince you insist on bringing in the Solar perfect dodge, let me remind you, Seven Shadow Evasion only requires Essence 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T11:48:37-07:00","id":1098170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1098155#post1098155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of those puzzles where you only see the picture when you put it together - if Becoming the Swarm and other &quot;become a swarm&quot; tricks are the territory of high-Essence Charms, <i>and </i>Lunars need to become a swarm to perfect dodge stuff, then <b>Lunars in your model won't be able to perfect dodge stuff until they're high-Essence</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the &quot;scattering perfect dodge Charm&quot; is a lower-Essence prerequisite for a higher-Essence &quot;remain scattered&quot; Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T13:36:03-07:00","id":1098213,"title":"","content":"Not sure if that's a good thing chances are dodgings going to be in dexterity or something like it<br /> <br /> Then again maybe because there multiple ways to do something on the Baseline the lunars can have multiple charms and different attributes that sort of have the same effect but lead to different developments?<br /> But that might run into the complaint that the lunars have too many charms that do the same thing<br /> Alchemical exalted have an easy because of the mentioned fact that they can only do so many at a time and requipment and power growth are detrimental for the kind of activities that a player character would want to take.<br /> Tw, would you be comfortable if lunars had redundant charms throughout different trees or attributes or how would you fit swarming with a more basic way of doing things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:38:38-07:00","id":1098249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darmani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1098213#post1098213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if that's a good thing chances are dodgings going to be in dexterity or something like it</div> </div> </div> </div>Every single Charm concept listed above is a Dexterity Charm.<br /> <br /> Vance has confirmed that Lunar Charms are going to handle shapeshifting. No need for Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T15:06:31-07:00","id":1098256,"title":"","content":"...<br /> Its good shapeshifting is part of the charm set. If so then I would actually... cheat. Again not 3rd ed guy.<br /> <br /> Make it so dodge dice or whatever defense is used is always applicable to attacks. The aesthetic is dodging like mister fantastic (or Dhalsim or a contortionist or whatever) thanks to mastery of form.<br /> Blades go into the lunar but while superficial amounts of blood get drawn like in a gladitorial combat nothing is hurt. Also can try for a disarm or getting the blade stuck. AFTER that build to swarming.<br /> <br /> That way Lunar's can do something brutal anime does, its based more on dodging and even something humans and freak/geeks did (stabbing self with objects with no real harm, catching bullets with teeth, and turning out of the way) at the low levels. In this movement/evasion set include the possibilty of spliting into parts or a swarm. THEN the advanced branch goes to swarm charms overall.<br /> <br /> Thank you for not expressing discourtesy at me for what I said about you, Sunder.<br /> <br /> And how is my suggestion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1097592-lunar-exalted-and-the-power-of-being-small?p=1098249#post1098249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single Charm concept listed above is a Dexterity Charm.<br /> <br /> Vance has confirmed that Lunar Charms are going to handle shapeshifting. No need for Knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm then again....if we go with butterfly dodge that would mean they could cheat/hack through none completely solid barriers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 05-29-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T04:09:41-07:00","id":1098393,"title":"","content":"The idea of a dodge being a prerequisite to or lead in for powers based on having scattered into a number of animals is interesting, but personally I would be averse to it functioning specifically in the manner of evading everything without contest. It may be a bit irrational, but in my mind it would create a certain sense of... elevating a certain aesthetic in the Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen talking about comparisons to perfect dodges in older systems to possibilities in the new one, I think it's worth noting that perfect defence has become a bit of holdover terminology that is actually in error now; both Heavenly Guardian Defence and Adamant Skin Technique can actually be overcome now, even if they're both pulling double duty as Charms that can be used to stop arbitrary uncountable damage effects. Seven Shadow Evasion could conceivably prove to be the only truly perfect dodge in the game, and even it is limited by the constraints of resetting it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSecond Edition pivoted a lot around perfect defences, but Third Edition has a bit more nuance in the functions of its combat, so while before other Exalted also had their shares of Charms that fully negated attacks or damage without contest, I would question the necessity of them this time around.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo given those premises, I would first ask what one envisioned when they were designating any given Charm as a splat defining perfect defence; is it like Third Edition's Seven Shadow Evasion, or its Adamant Skin Technique?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf the best that Lunars had was more like the latter, then I think there would be more from breaking into a swarm and being highly reactive and flexible being just different, rather than one strictly superior to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T08:30:10-07:00","id":1098441,"title":"","content":"Here I must bow out, enjoy y'all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}